      "latency_ms": 8127.745583071373,
      "tokens": 5034,
      "cost_usd": 0.0007974,
      "answer": "NVIDIA identifies the risk that restrictions imposed by the Chinese government on the duration of gaming activities and access to games may adversely affect their Gaming revenue, and increased oversight of digital platform companies may adversely affect their Data Center revenue. Additionally, the Chinese government may encourage customers to purchase from China-based competitors or impose restrictions on the sale to certain customers of their products, which could negatively impact their business and financial results [c:NVDA_2025_1A_39]."
    },
    {
      "id": "q027",
      "type": "risk_narrative",
      "recall": 1.0,
      "mrr": 0.2,
      "citation_precision": 1.0,
      "must_refuse": false,
      "actually_refused": false,
      "refusal_correct": true,
      "grounded": true,
      "latency_ms": 8876.94229092449,
      "tokens": 4786,
      "cost_usd": 0.0007521,
      "answer": "JPMorgan Chase identifies the following broad categories of risk factors in its 10-K:\n\n1. Liquidity risks\n2. Capital risks\n3. Operational risks\n4. Strategic risks\n5. Conduct risks\n6. Reputation risks\n7. Country risks\n8. People risks\n9. Legal risks [c:JPM_2023_1A_1]."
    },
    {
      "id": "q028",
      "type": "risk_narrative",
      "recall": 1.0,
      "mrr": 1.0,
      "citation_precision": 1.0,
      "must_refuse": false,
      "actually_refused": false,
      "refusal_correct": true,
      "grounded": true,
      "latency_ms": 8948.692708974704,
      "tokens": 4673,
      "cost_usd": 0.0007473,
      "answer": "Apple discloses that its operations and performance depend significantly on global and regional economic conditions, and that adverse economic conditions can materially adversely affect the Company\u2019s business, results of operations, financial condition, and stock price. Specific adverse macroeconomic conditions mentioned include slow growth or recession, high unemployment, inflation, tighter credit, higher interest rates, and currency fluctuations, which can adversely impact consumer confidence and spending, thereby affecting demand for the Company\u2019s products and services [c:AAPL_2025_1A_0]."
    },
    {
      "id": "q029",
      "type": "risk_narrative",
      "recall": 1.0,
      "mrr": 1.0,
      "citation_precision": 1.0,
      "must_refuse": false,
      "actually_refused": false,
      "refusal_correct": true,
      "grounded": true,
      "latency_ms": 8810.672833002172,
      "tokens": 4257,
      "cost_usd": 0.00069255,
      "answer": "Apple discloses that its new products often utilize custom components available from only one source, which can lead to significant risks of supply shortages and price increases. The Company may not be able to extend or renew agreements for the supply of components on similar terms, or at all, and may not be successful in obtaining sufficient quantities from its suppliers in a timely manner, or in identifying and obtaining sufficient quantities from an alternative source. This reliance on single-source components can materially adversely affect its business, results of operations, financial condition, and stock price [c:AAPL_2025_1A_8]."
    },
    {
      "id": "q030",
      "type": "risk_narrative",
      "recall": 0.0,
      "mrr": 0.0,
      "citation_precision": 1.0,
